{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"Replacing the global fixed-point semantics with a local proof-tree search redefines the semantics rather than expanding it, violating the target standard. The proposal explicitly makes the fixed point a mere sanity check, undermining the requirement to preserve and strengthen the existing skeptical fixed-point semantics of spec §4.","target":"08badabf4487bd4a36562e1568030ef05e1ac2ecba2f13ad73f22c797ee8f942"},{"attack":true,"case":"The proposal explicitly acknowledges that reinstatement may become non-structural under a semiring of evidence. Since the target standard mandates preserving reinstatement as a derived property, this admitted failure means the proposal violates the core requirements of the problem.","target":"8a5d68597282aa52e291867b5adc95770d486650530adf75559dfb0c1a356884"},{"attack":true,"case":"The proposal explicitly acknowledges that sensitivity analysis could become exponential unless restricted to local perturbations. The target standard strictly requires preserving polynomial cost. By leaving the polynomial-time guarantee contingent on an unimplemented local restriction, the proposal fails to ensure the required complexity bound.","target":"9d630d280569f9f6db3f5d06b50bd7826a9647ecbb77b6cda95a2d2ec592a4b8"}]}